<title>FRANCE: Lille airport Jan-June cargo traffic up 13 pct.</title>
<headline>Lille airport Jan-June cargo traffic up 13 pct.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lille-Lesquin Airport, in northern France, handled 13,243 tonnes of cargo traffic in the first six months of 1997, an increase of 13 percent on 1996 levels, airport authority figures show.</p>
<p>The increase in traffic was largely down to double-digit growth in traffic handled by Air France, DHL, French handling agents, France Handling and SFS and Belgian carrier, Sabena, the airport authority added. - Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel+ 44 171 542 7706 Fax +5017 - www.racs.com</p>
</text>
